  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance for Displaced People in the Lake Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of January 2023, there were more than 255,054 displaced persons in 245 localities in the Lac province of Chad. This includes people recently displaced by the floods in August 2022 and those who have been displaced for a prolonged period of time. According to assessments conducted by the International Organization for Migration (IOM) in December 2022, the floods had completed completely or partially destroyed many houses, leaving those affected homeless or forced to stay with host families. To meet the needs of displaced populations in Lac province, IOM is building emergency shelters for the most vulnerable (female-headed households, families with individuals with disabilities, large households). IOM is further contributing to the overall response through the use of biometric data to inform the Food Security Cluster and its partners of the nutritional needs of displaced persons.</narrative>
  </description>
